cache: disk 96G, 6.4 GB allocated; attached to the running VM, on caboose-vmm's own disk (resizes while it runs)
  vm.big               /home/agent/.cache/go-build  128G
  vm.default (in use)  /home/agent/.cache/go-build  64G
data: no disk yet: a VM of a profile that declares it makes it as it starts
  vm.default (in use)  /data  8G
old: disk 32G, 2.1 GB allocated; no profile declares it: 'caboose volume rm old --delete-disk' deletes it
web: disk 4G, 268 MB allocated; only container and gvisor profiles declare it, which attach no disk
  container.default  /srv/web  -
docker: dockerd's disk, 64G, 4.3 GB allocated (docker_size in [vm.default]: 64G); 'caboose prune --docker' empties it
TMP/.caboose/envs/default/data/vm/volumes/.cache.img.restoring-1700000000000000000 (0G, 0 B allocated) is a copy of a checkpoint that an interrupted restore of volume cache left (the checkpoint keeps it): 'rm TMP/.caboose/envs/default/data/vm/volumes/.cache.img.restoring-1700000000000000000' deletes it
TMP/.caboose/envs/default/data/vm/volumes/cache.img.before-shrink (0G, 0 B allocated) is a shrink's backup of volume cache's disk: 'rm TMP/.caboose/envs/default/data/vm/volumes/cache.img.before-shrink' deletes it once you no longer need it
TMP/.caboose/envs/default/data/vm/volumes/old.img.before-restore is volume old's disk itself under a second name, which a restore interrupted before its last step left: 'rm TMP/.caboose/envs/default/data/vm/volumes/old.img.before-restore' removes the name, not the disk (the next restore removes it too)
TMP/.caboose/envs/default/data/vm/volumes/web.img.before-restore (2G, 134 MB allocated) is volume web's disk as it was before a checkpoint's restore: once the volume is right, 'rm TMP/.caboose/envs/default/data/vm/volumes/web.img.before-restore' deletes it; to undo the restore instead, with the VM stopped, 'mv TMP/.caboose/envs/default/data/vm/volumes/web.img.before-restore TMP/.caboose/envs/default/data/vm/volumes/web.img'
